# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AUTHZ - STALE SESSION AND CROSS-ORIGIN REJECTION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verified against the source before writing this file:
# - AuthEndpoints.Logout.cs: logout revokes the active refresh token row, denylists the current
#   access token JTI, and deletes both auth cookies, so a session used after logout is rejected
#   whether or not the client still holds the old cookie values.
# - Middleware/UnsafeCookieRequestOriginMiddleware.cs: any unsafe method (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE)
#   under /api/** that carries an auth cookie is rejected with 403 Forbidden when the Origin header
#   does not match the configured WebUI origin - this runs before the auth pipeline consumes the
#   cookie, so a rejected request leaves the session untouched.
#
# tests/API/auth/session-lifecycle.http already proves "Validate after logout (401 expected)", and
# tests/API/auth/origin-csrf.http already proves the foreign-Origin-rejected-403 and
# missing-Origin-rejected-403 cases on /api/auth/refresh and /api/auth/logout. Both scenarios are
# repeated here, with the admin account and the literal example origin from the audit
# item, so this dedicated authz suite is self-contained.
# Signs in with the admin account: the admin is a mechanic person too (person_type mechanic), so it
# passes MechanicOnly, and nothing in this file depends on the Admin role.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@SessionEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@SessionPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@ForeignOrigin = https://evil.example.com


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [Setup][Authz] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup][Authz] Login with the admin account
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{SessionEmail}}",
  "password": "{{SessionPassword}}"
}

?? status == 200

###

### [Positive][Authz] Session is authenticated before logout (200 expected)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/validate

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Authz] Logout (204 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

?? status == 204

###

### [Negative][Authz] Replaying a request with the now-stale post-logout cookies is rejected (401 expected)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/validate

?? status == 401

###

### [Setup][Authz] Login with the admin account again for the cross-origin check
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{SessionEmail}}",
  "password": "{{SessionPassword}}"
}

?? status == 200

###

### [Negative][Authz] Cross-origin unsafe request with a foreign Origin and valid cookies is rejected (403 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{ForeignOrigin}}

?? status == 403

###

### [Positive][Authz] Session survives the rejected cross-origin attempt (200 expected, still logged in)
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/validate

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Authz] Logout with the correct Origin (204 expected, cleanup)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

?? status == 204
